++ duplicate card sends
++MIME-Version: 1.0
++Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
++Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
++
++The deliver callback is async — while it awaits runMessageSending (the
++message_sending plugin hook), the dispatcher's onIdle fires from
++markDispatchIdle() and closes the streaming card. When deliver resumes,
++streaming is null so it falls through to the non-streaming path, sending
++a second card with the hook-rewritten content.
++
++Fix: guard onIdle with a deliverInFlight flag so it defers closeStreaming
++while the deliver callback is awaiting the hook. Also capture
++streamingWasActive before the await so deliver still takes the streaming
++path even if onIdle sneaks in.
++
++Additionally, normalize hook-appended <at user_id> tags to card-compatible
++<at id> format before streaming.close() so @mentions render as blue links.
++
++Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
